    "q-113186": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113186",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150837/assets/b9e5d7d183fb090b317bd134829affc63792fbe88945941d5be1311e27751afb.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Note that $A$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we deduce that $A$ corresponds to $2\\,\\text{in}$ while $B$ corresponds to $3.5\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB=3.5\\,\\text{in}-2\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
