      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150837/assets/5349fd8cce4fc4c31f4ddf54616158cc9bc1755b78011bdbc699fd5253524382.png)\n\nFind the length of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that $A$ corresponds to $-4$ units while $B$ corresponds to $1$ units.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nAB=1-(-4)=5\\,\\text{units}.\n$$",
